{"id":"systemd-portabled.service.8","n":"systemd-portabled.service","s":"8","src":{"u":{"pkg":"systemd-container","ver":"249.11-0ubuntu3.23","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/s/systemd/systemd-container_249.11-0ubuntu3.23_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/systemd-portabled.service.8.gz","sha256":"b3c03ea226829a6d877a03d9968a438763357d38c3884745747e035b27036d1a","date":"","origin":"systemd 249"}},"nopt":{"u":0},"desc":"Portable service manager","u":[["NAME","<p>systemd-portabled.service, systemd-portabled - Portable service manager</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p>systemd-portabled.service</p> <p>/lib/systemd/systemd-portabled</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><b>systemd-portabled</b> is a system service that may be used to attach, detach and inspect portable service images.</p> <p>Most of <b>systemd-portabled</b>'s functionality is accessible through the <b>portablectl</b>(1) command.</p> <p>See <b>Portable Services</b>[1] for details about the concepts this service implements.</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>systemd</b>(1), <b>portablectl</b>(1), <b>org.freedesktop.portable1</b>(5)</p>"],["NOTES","<dl><dt>1.</dt><dd>Portable Services</dd></dl> <div class=\"in\">https://systemd.io/PORTABLE_SERVICES</div>"]]}